import Base from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>Java Quick Reference</h1>

<p>
    This is the exact reference sheet distributed with the AP Computer Science
    A exam, effective Fall 2025, reproduced from the CED appendix. You will
    hold a printout of this in the exam room. Train with it all year: print
    it, fold it, mark it up, and never write a method from memory that you
    could look up in fifteen seconds.
</p>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>Speed drills:</strong> every lesson marked "JQR drill" gives you 3
    minutes to find a method on this sheet and use it cold. The exam is 42
    questions in 90 minutes: retrieval speed is scoring speed.
</div>

<h2>String Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String(String str)</code></td><td>Constructs a new String object that represents the same sequence of characters as str</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>int length()</code></td><td>Returns the number of characters in a String object</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String substring(int from, int to)</code></td><td>Returns the substring beginning at index from and ending at index to-1</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String substring(int from)</code></td><td>Returns substring(from, length())</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>int indexOf(String str)</code></td><td>Returns the index of the first occurrence of str; returns -1 if not found</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>boolean equals(Object other)</code></td><td>Returns true if this corresponds to the same sequence of characters as other; returns false otherwise</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>int compareTo(String other)</code></td><td>Returns a value &lt;0 if this is less than other; returns zero if this is equal to other; returns a value &gt;0 if this is greater than other. Strings are ordered based upon the alphabet.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String[] split(String del)</code></td><td>Returns a String array where each element is a substring of this String, which has been split around matches of the given expression del</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Integer Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Integer.MIN_VALUE</code></td><td>The minimum value represented by an int or Integer</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Integer.MAX_VALUE</code></td><td>The maximum value represented by an int or Integer</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static int parseInt(String s)</code></td><td>Returns the String argument as an int</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static double parseDouble(String s)</code></td><td>Returns the String argument as a double</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Math Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static int abs(int x)</code></td><td>Returns the absolute value of an int value</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static double abs(double x)</code></td><td>Returns the absolute value of a double value</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static double pow(double base, double exponent)</code></td><td>Returns the value of the first parameter raised to the power of the second parameter</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static double sqrt(double x)</code></td><td>Returns the correctly rounded positive square root of a double value</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>static double random()</code></td><td>Returns a double value greater than or equal to 0.0 and less than 1.0</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>ArrayList&lt;E&gt; Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>int size()</code></td><td>Returns the number of elements in the list</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>boolean add(E obj)</code></td><td>Appends obj to end of list; returns true</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>void add(int index, E obj)</code></td><td>Inserts obj at position index (0&lt;=index&lt;=size), moving elements at position index and higher to the right (adds 1 to their indices) and adds 1 to size</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>E get(int index)</code></td><td>Returns the element at position index in the list</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>E set(int index, E obj)</code></td><td>Replaces the element at position index with obj; returns the element formerly at position index</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>E remove(int index)</code></td><td>Removes element from position index, moving elements at position index+1 and higher to the left (subtracts 1 from their indices) and subtracts 1 from size; returns the element formerly at position index</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>File Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>File(String pathname)</code></td><td>The File constructor that accepts a String pathname</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Scanner Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Scanner(File f)</code></td><td>The Scanner constructor that accepts a File for reading</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>int nextInt()</code></td><td>Returns the next int read from the file or input source if available. If the next int does not exist or is out of range, it will result in an InputMismatchException.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>double nextDouble()</code></td><td>Returns the next double read from the file or input source. If the next double does not exist, it will result in an InputMismatchException.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>boolean nextBoolean()</code></td><td>Returns the next boolean read from the file or input source. If the next boolean does not exist, it will result in an InputMismatchException.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String nextLine()</code></td><td>Returns the next line of text as a String read from the file or input source; can return the empty string if called immediately after another Scanner method that is reading from the file or input source</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String next()</code></td><td>Returns the next String read from the file or input source</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>boolean hasNext()</code></td><td>Returns true if there is a next item to read in the file or input source; false otherwise</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>void close()</code></td><td>Closes this scanner</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Object Class</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Class Constructors and Methods</th><th>Explanation</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>boolean equals(Object other)</code></td><td>Returns true if this and other are the same object; otherwise returns false</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String toString()</code></td><td>Returns a String representation of this object</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="callout warn">
    <strong>What is deliberately NOT on the sheet:</strong> String.trim,
    String.toUpperCase, String.toLowerCase, String.contains,
    String.startsWith, charAt, toCharArray, the two-argument
    indexOf(String, int), the Character and Boolean classes, StringBuilder,
    String.format, System.out.printf, most of ArrayList (contains, indexOf,
    addAll, clear, isEmpty), Collections.sort, the Arrays class, Math.max,
    Math.min, Math.round, arrays.length and 2D array bounds (the sheet has no
    array section at all, so these you simply know), and any I/O beyond
    the File/Scanner basics above.
    The table below gives the substitute for the ones you will actually
    reach for. Anything not on the sheet that a question needs will be
    described in the question itself. If a question uses a method you do not
    recognize, the question defines it: read the definition, it is the whole
    point.
</div>

<h2>Methods You Will Reach For, and What to Write Instead</h2>

<p>
    Every entry here works in Java and none of them is on the sheet. Learn the
    right-hand column now, while you have a compiler in front of you, so that
    on exam day your fingers write the version that runs.
</p>

<table>
    <tr><th>Not on the sheet</th><th>Write this instead</th></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.contains(t)</code></td><td><code>s.indexOf(t) != -1</code>. <code>0</code> means found at the very start, which is a hit</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.trim()</code></td><td>Nothing on the sheet removes whitespace. Trim in a loop with <code>indexOf</code> and <code>substring</code>, or keep the spaces out in the first place</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.charAt(i)</code></td><td><code>s.substring(i, i + 1)</code>, a one-character String you can compare with <code>equals</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.equalsIgnoreCase(t)</code></td><td><code>s.toLowerCase().equals(t.toLowerCase())</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.startsWith(t)</code></td><td><code>s.indexOf(t) == 0</code>, the same "found at the very start" fact the contains row turns on</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.isEmpty()</code></td><td><code>s.length() == 0</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.toUpperCase()</code>, <code>s.toLowerCase()</code></td><td>No substitute. Chain them onto <code>equals</code> or <code>indexOf</code> when you need case-insensitive work</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>s.indexOf(t, from)</code></td><td><code>s.substring(first + 1).indexOf(t) + first + 1</code>, the second occurrence built out of the first</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>String.format(f, x)</code></td><td>Concatenation. Build any padding yourself</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>System.out.printf(f, x)</code></td><td>Concatenation again, with the spacing built by hand</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Character.isDigit(ch)</code></td><td>Get the one-character String first, then compare: <code>ch.compareTo("0") &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; ch.compareTo("9") &lt;= 0</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Character.isLetter(ch)</code></td><td>The same idea with two ranges: <code>(ch.compareTo("A") &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; ch.compareTo("Z") &lt;= 0) || (ch.compareTo("a") &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; ch.compareTo("z") &lt;= 0)</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Math.max(a, b)</code>, <code>Math.min(a, b)</code></td><td>An <code>if</code>. Chasing a running max in a loop? Start at <code>Integer.MIN_VALUE</code> and replace when you find something bigger</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Math.round(x)</code></td><td>Not on the sheet either. If the value cannot be negative, add 0.5 and cast: <code>(int) (x + 0.5)</code>. Negative halves round differently, so handle those deliberately</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>list.contains(obj)</code></td><td>A loop with <code>equals</code>, returning true when you find it</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>list.indexOf(obj)</code></td><td>The same loop, tracking the index</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>list.isEmpty()</code></td><td><code>list.size() == 0</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>list.clear()</code></td><td>Remove in a loop, or hand back a new <code>ArrayList</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>list.addAll(other)</code></td><td>A loop with <code>add</code>, one element at a time</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>list.remove(obj)</code></td><td>The sheet's <code>remove</code> takes an index, not an object. Find the index with the <code>equals</code> loop, then call <code>remove(int)</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Collections.sort(list)</code>, <code>Arrays.sort(arr)</code></td><td>Write the sort. Unit 7's sorting page builds both of them</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Arrays.copyOfRange(arr, from, to)</code>, and the rest of the Arrays class</td><td>Nothing from Arrays is on the sheet. Copy by hand into a new array with a <code>for</code> loop</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>StringBuilder</code></td><td><code>+=</code> on a String</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Boolean.parseBoolean(s)</code></td><td>The Boolean class is not on the sheet. Compare instead: <code>s.equals("true")</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Scanner.hasNextInt()</code></td><td><code>hasNext()</code> plus <code>next()</code> and <code>parseInt</code>, or let <code>nextInt()</code> throw and catch it</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>f.exists()</code></td><td>Not on the sheet. A question that needs it will say so</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Reading Speed Targets</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>Drill</th><th>Target</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Find any class's table</td><td>under 15 seconds</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Signature to plain English</td><td>under 30 seconds</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Spot the return type trap (set/remove return values)</td><td>on sight</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Write the hasNext/nextLine loop from memory</td><td>under 60 seconds, correct first time</td></tr>
</table>`;
